+## 14. Conversation list
+
+A client MAY send `list_conversations` with an optional integer `limit` from 1 through 200 and an optional
+`before` cursor containing an ISO `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`; incomplete or invalid fields receive
+`INVALID_MESSAGE` even when history is disabled ([validated by: validates list_conversations limits and complete ISO cursors before history is enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L96)).
+
+When `transport.history.enabled` is true, the server answers `list_conversations` with one `conversation_list`
+frame containing newest-first `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount` summaries. The two times are
+ISO strings, the current connection's session is included, no conversation content is sent, and the query uses the
+authenticated connection user rather than any field on the frame ([validated by: delivers only the connecting users newest conversation summaries as ISO wire values](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L119)).
+
+The server passes a supplied `limit` and composite `before` cursor unchanged to the authenticated user's `listFor`
+query ([validated by: forwards a bounded page and its composite cursor to the authenticated users store query](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L166)).
+
+When history is disabled or the configured store has no `listFor`, the server returns `UNSUPPORTED`, not an empty
+`conversation_list` ([validated by: reports UNSUPPORTED rather than an empty list when history is disabled or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L183)).
